# The red control of the judge of cells. A literal with a spread is filled in sight: what stands between the copy and the definitions is walked in front of the tests of the form and again in its closed arm.
# A closure that somebody else holds too may not stand there: it would be made twice on the way through the closed arm, and `made.read === kept` would be false, in silence: plain Bun prints true.
# THE LIE is the command walk-where-every-closure-stands-behind-copies, which no build can say: every closure may stand there.
# Where code is verified, Walker::build() notes an operation of the body that is given a second cell in one walk of its block. Behind the sweep the build stops by name where both cells are needed, no way reaches
# the second but through the block of the first, and the first is used behind the second before its own block is passed again: two cells stand for one operation at one time.
# DIAGNOSTIC: OperationMakesTwoCells
# RUN: walk-where-every-closure-stands-behind-copies f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: the walk of f1:Body failed
